TI  - The P versus NP Problem in Quantum Physics
T2  - NEUROQUANTOLOGY
LA  - English
KW  - NP problem
KW  - polynomial
AB  - Motivated by the fact that information is encoded and processed by physical systems, the P versus NP problem is examined in terms of physical processes. In particular, we consider P as a class of deterministic, and NP as nondeterministic, polynomial-time physical processes. Based on these identifications, we review a self-reference physical process in quantum theory, which belongs to NP but cannot be contained in P.
